22.11. Rodrigues' Formula
f_{n}(x)=\frac{1}{a_{n\rho}(x)}\frac{d^{n}}{dx^{n}}(\rho(x)(g(x))^{n})
The polynomials given in the following table are the only orthogonal polynomials which satisfy this formula.

\begin{tabular}{c c c c c}  & f_{n}(x) & a_{n} & \rho(x) & g(x) \\
22.11.1 & P_{n}^{(\mu,\,\beta)}(x) & (-1)^{-2}n! & (1-x)^{n}(1+x)^{\beta} & 1-x^{1} \\
22.11.2 & C_{n}^{(\alpha)}(x) & (-1)^{-2}n! & (1-x)^{n}(1+x)^{\beta} & 1-x^{1} \\
22.11.3 & T_{n}(x) & (-1)^{-2}n! & \frac{T(n+\tfrac{1}{2})}{\sqrt\pi} & (1-x)^{n-1} & 1-x^{2} \\
22.11.4 & U_{n}(x) & (-1)^{-2}n! & \frac{T(n+\tfrac{1}{2})}{(n+1)\sqrt\pi} & (1-x)^{1} & 1-x^{2} \\
22.11.5 & P_{n}(x) & (-1)^{-2}n! & 1 & 1-x^{2} \\
22.11.6 & L_{n}^{(\alpha)}(x) & n! & \frac{1}{n!} & \frac{1-x^{2}}{x} \\
22.11.7 & H_{n}(x) & (-1)^{n} & e^{-x^{2}} & 1 \\
22.11.8 & H_{n}(x) & (-1)^{n} & e^{-x^{2}/n} & 1 \\ \end{tabular}
